# What borgmatic leaves out of $HOME: reproducible bulk, caches, and anything re-downloadable.
# Borg patterns, see `borg help patterns`; borgmatic expands a leading ~ but nothing else, so ~ anchors an entry at $HOME.
# `!` excludes without descending, so a huge excluded tree costs nothing to skip.
# The default style is sh:, where `*` stops at a slash; a `**/` prefix is what lets a bare name match at any depth.
# A trailing slash would keep the directory and drop only its contents, so none of these has one.
# Folders holding a CACHEDIR.TAG or a .nobackup file are dropped by config.yaml, not here.

